title: 'P8-D86..D88: tighten by cutting autonomy, start strict with one-click modes, loosen on evidence + Touch ID'
summary: The founder resolved the research 35/36 divergence and both open questions. These rulings feed spec v3.9 part 2 and the M1.1 contract reservations (research 35 A35-20 + research 36 reserve list, merged).
symbols_touched:
  - '#approval-broker'
  - '#gui'
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D86
    decision: Gate tightening cuts agent autonomy, not the founder's time (Aegis S35-07, CB4). Tightening means fewer agents in parallel, auto-merge off, cached-class decisions become fresh-presence for that repo, and voice narrowed (grant ∩ breaker); it never adds cards per decision. Extra verdicts only on high-risk / gate-class changes. Arky's 'verdict on every node at L2' is dropped.
    rationale: 'Founder: more cards lead to rubber-stamping; spend autonomy, not attention.'
  - id: P8-D87
    decision: Repos whose reviewer is not yet calibrated start at strictness L1. Strictness and the related modes (manual / ask / auto-edits, akin to Claude Code's permission modes) are one-click in Gnomon (GUI control + command palette + per-repo/per-session), as easy as or easier than Claude Code's. Tightening is one click with no presence; loosening is one click plus the Touch ID prompt (D88).
    rationale: 'Founder: yes start at L1, but changing strictness and modes like Claude Code''s edits/auto/manual must be as easy if not easier to click in Gnomon.'
  - id: P8-D88
    decision: Loosening requires positive evidence (survived merged work, oracle passes, never mere quiet time, S35-02) plus elapsed dwell, one level at a time, each step confirmed with fresh presence (Touch ID); going below what the evidence supports needs the root key and counts as an override.
    rationale: Founder chose evidence + Touch ID.
